{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Proportional Reasoning-1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.706,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "The ratio of the counters of your partner to yours is 5 : 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.111,
            0.848,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "? Now, if you want to share the counters between the two of you in the ratio of 3 : 1, how many counters would each of you get?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.153,
            0.848,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": "Share the counters in different ways and see which combination is in the ratio 3 : 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.19,
            0.806,
            0.21
          ],
          "content": "One way to share the counters in the ratio of 3 : 1 is as follows —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.215,
            0.848,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "1. Your partner takes 3 counters and you take 1 counter. There are now 8 counters left."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.256,
            0.846,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "2. Your partner takes 3 more counters and you take 1 more counter. There are now 4 counters left."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.299,
            0.847,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": "3. Your partner takes 3 more counters and you take 1 more counter. There are no more counters left."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.341,
            0.769,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "So, your partner gets 9 counters in total and you get 3 counters."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.36,
            0.846,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": "When we divide 12 counters in the ratio of 3 : 1 between two people, one gets 9 counters and the other gets 3 counters."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.4,
            0.851,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.657,
            0.847,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": "？ Now, if you want to share 42 counters between the two of you in the ratio of 4 : 3, how will you do it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.7,
            0.847,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "Using the same procedure would take a long time! There is a simpler way to share the whole with parts in a specified ratio."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.738,
            0.848,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": "You need to divide 42 into groups such that your partner gets 4 groups and you get 3 groups."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.781,
            0.458,
            0.805
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "What is the size of each group?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.81,
            0.847,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "If your partner gets 4 groups and you get 3 groups, the total number of groups is 7. So, the size of each group is 42 ÷ 7 = 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.847,
            0.848,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": "Multiplying the number of groups by the size of each group, your partner gets 24 counters and you get 18 counters, when you share 42 counters in the ratio of 4 : 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.872,
            0.914,
            0.919,
            0.937
          ],
          "content": "173"
        }
      ]
    }
